{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":10022254,"name":"blutzer","username":"blutzer","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/devforum.roblox.com/blutzer/{size}/5000391_2.png","created_at":"2024-02-13T20:00:00.000Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eIf you’re looking to create screenshots or videos for promotional material, experience thumbnails, or to document your experience in any way, these tips will help you capture your work at its best. This content gives you quick guidance on:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eMaximizing your \u003ca href=\"https://devforum.roblox.com/t/tips-for-capturing-high-quality-screenshots-and-videos-in-studio/2723897#image-and-rendering-settings-1\"\u003eimage and rendering settings\u003c/a\u003e in Studio\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSetting up \u003ca href=\"https://devforum.roblox.com/t/tips-for-capturing-high-quality-screenshots-and-videos-in-studio/2723897#obs-settings-5\"\u003escreen recording\u003c/a\u003e with OBS\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eUsing the \u003ca href=\"https://devforum.roblox.com/t/tips-for-capturing-high-quality-screenshots-and-videos-in-studio/2723897#using-free-camera-10\"\u003ebuilt-in free camera mode\u003c/a\u003e to showcase your experience\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo follow along, make sure you have Roblox Studio installed and OBS (\u003ca href=\"https://obsproject.com/\"\u003eOpen Broadcaster Software\u003c/a\u003e) for screen recording.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"/secure-uploads/uploads/original/5X/a/0/5/b/a05b10eee87d04c32869997ccc1066cf2b02ddef.jpeg\" data-download-href=\"/uploads/short-url/mSzvdNh04jqvUfCGP8A0ywblaOz.jpeg?dl=1\" title=\"Capturing High Quality Screenshots in Studio\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://devforum.roblox.com/secure-uploads/uploads/optimized/5X/a/0/5/b/a05b10eee87d04c32869997ccc1066cf2b02ddef_2_686x500.jpeg\" alt=\"Capturing High Quality Screenshots in Studio\" data-base62-sha1=\"mSzvdNh04jqvUfCGP8A0ywblaOz\" width=\"686\" height=\"500\" srcset=\"https://devforum.roblox.com/secure-uploads/uploads/optimized/5X/a/0/5/b/a05b10eee87d04c32869997ccc1066cf2b02ddef_2_686x500.jpeg, https://devforum.roblox.com/secure-uploads/uploads/optimized/5X/a/0/5/b/a05b10eee87d04c32869997ccc1066cf2b02ddef_2_1029x750.jpeg 1.5x, https://devforum.roblox.com/secure-uploads/uploads/original/5X/a/0/5/b/a05b10eee87d04c32869997ccc1066cf2b02ddef.jpeg 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"577383\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"meta\"\u003e\n\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#far-image\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003cspan class=\"filename\"\u003eCapturing High Quality Screenshots in Studio\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"informations\"\u003e1324×964 90.7 KB\u003c/span\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#discourse-expand\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch1\u003e\n\u003ca name=\"image-and-rendering-settings-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#image-and-rendering-settings-1\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eImage and Rendering Settings\u003c/h1\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo ensure your screenshots and videos are visually stunning, it’s essential to maximize your rendering settings. While Roblox automatically adjusts rendering quality to balance between performance and quality, you can temporarily adjust these values to ensure you’re capturing your experience in its highest fidelity. Use the following tips to ensure your experience looks great:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\n\u003ca name=\"in-studio-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#in-studio-2\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eIn Studio\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo maximize your graphic quality in Studio:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eNavigate to File \u0026gt; Studio settings and click the Rendering Tab.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSet Editor Quality to 21.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSet Mesh Detail Level to Level00.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cimg src=\"/secure-uploads/uploads/original/5X/2/a/5/7/2a57410654a1affb7c301d4a2218ec4ab70833cc.png\" alt=\"\" data-base62-sha1=\"62yZFevfJE3XNw0UqoSQuafKIKU\" width=\"438\" height=\"500\" role=\"presentation\"\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003ch4\u003e\n\u003ca name=\"during-runtime-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#during-runtime-3\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDuring Runtime\u003c/h4\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo maximize your graphics quality while joining or testing a Roblox experience:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ePress Escape or the Start button on a controller to get to the Player menu.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSet Graphics Mode to Manual.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSet Graphics Quality to its maximum level.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cimg src=\"/secure-uploads/uploads/original/5X/c/1/1/5/c115d13f6b747869831d38109f87b806a33006db.png\" alt=\"\" data-base62-sha1=\"ry6TvycsYCRPMDQJ0POe8cz5eWf\" width=\"689\" height=\"425\" role=\"presentation\"\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\n\u003ca name=\"setting-and-saving-resolutions-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#setting-and-saving-resolutions-4\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSetting and Saving Resolutions\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhen showcasing your experience and trying to engage new users, it’s important to showcase how your experience may look on different devices. Use the following steps to quickly change and save resolution settings:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn Studio, navigate to the Test tab and select Device.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cimg src=\"/secure-uploads/uploads/original/5X/4/3/7/b/437b9f35a095700c388d670aa7c262485aa3c798.png\" alt=\"\" data-base62-sha1=\"9CYQEuT6PtyVhQ2uVme1CHkPqc0\" width=\"262\" height=\"141\" role=\"presentation\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAbove your viewport, click the resolution dropdown and select your desired device and resolution. This also affects the resolution when testing your experience.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cimg src=\"/secure-uploads/uploads/original/5X/2/3/e/c/23ecb84a64b26fe92ee9006ad48a74b72b8e1a3e.png\" alt=\"\" data-base62-sha1=\"57NSEpvIdif0Qz0EuoeT7ZuOzUO\" width=\"689\" height=\"421\" role=\"presentation\"\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cimg src=\"/secure-uploads/uploads/original/5X/5/6/a/9/56a98239aeac188c0fc10a3b63f5fe3e0bb83133.png\" alt=\"\" data-base62-sha1=\"cmEesg0Qhxipv9KSuU5Hpzmniwz\" width=\"689\" height=\"360\" role=\"presentation\"\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\n\u003ca name=\"how-to-take-the-screenshot-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#how-to-take-the-screenshot-5\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eHow To Take The Screenshot\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNow, when everything is set up as you like. Let’s do the actual Screenshot. To do this, let’s go to the VIEW Tab – and Click The Screen Shot Icon, please see the screenshot below.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"/secure-uploads/uploads/original/5X/8/5/1/d/851d0ac23063c959651aabfbbfb2ac23640eb58d.jpeg\" data-download-href=\"/uploads/short-url/iZzJ03QmHArXY7F3FKuIXVVGslD.jpeg?dl=1\" title=\"How To Take The Screenshot\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://devforum.roblox.com/secure-uploads/uploads/optimized/5X/8/5/1/d/851d0ac23063c959651aabfbbfb2ac23640eb58d_2_690x453.jpeg\" alt=\"How To Take The Screenshot\" data-base62-sha1=\"iZzJ03QmHArXY7F3FKuIXVVGslD\" width=\"690\" height=\"453\" srcset=\"https://devforum.roblox.com/secure-uploads/uploads/optimized/5X/8/5/1/d/851d0ac23063c959651aabfbbfb2ac23640eb58d_2_690x453.jpeg, https://devforum.roblox.com/secure-uploads/uploads/optimized/5X/8/5/1/d/851d0ac23063c959651aabfbbfb2ac23640eb58d_2_1035x679.jpeg 1.5x, https://devforum.roblox.com/secure-uploads/uploads/optimized/5X/8/5/1/d/851d0ac23063c959651aabfbbfb2ac23640eb58d_2_1380x906.jpeg 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"5F757D\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"meta\"\u003e\n\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#far-image\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003cspan class=\"filename\"\u003eHow To Take The Screenshot\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"informations\"\u003e1869×1229 176 KB\u003c/span\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#discourse-expand\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOnce clicked, your screenshot will be automatically saved in the default output folder. Which is within your computer’s profile Pictures Folder.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\n\u003ca name=\"any-other-help-needed-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#any-other-help-needed-6\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eAny other help needed?\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf you’re still scratching your head, don’t hesitate to drop a comment below. Got more questions? Ask away! Whether it’s about screenshots or anything else, I’m here to help. Let’s tackle those Roblox Studio challenges together!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch1\u003e\n\u003ca name=\"using-free-camera-7\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#using-free-camera-7\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eUsing Free Camera\u003c/h1\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhile testing experiences in Studio, you can use the free camera to disconnect the camera from your avatar and explore your environment using keyboard or controller movement. While testing an experience during runtime, press Shift + P to toggle the free camera and F11 to go full screen.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUse the following tips to get the most out of the free camera mode whether you are using a mouse or controller:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor mouse and keyboard:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eHold and drag right-click to pan.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eUse WASDEQ/UHJKIY to move\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eUse the mouse wheel to adjust field of view\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eUse the up \u0026amp; down arrows to adjust movement speed.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor controller:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eLeft analog stick - Dolly left/right, truck forward/backward\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRight analog stick - pan left/right, tilt up/down\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eLeft Trigger - crane down\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRight Trigger - crane up\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eGamepad Top Button (Y) - zoom in/decrease FOV\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eGamepad Left Button (X) - zoom out/increase FOV\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAdditional Hotkeys:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ePress L CTRL + L SHIFT + C to toggle basic UI visibility\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ePress L CTRL + L SHIFT to exit the free camera mode\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNo matter what type of media you’re creating, experiment with different camera angles, lighting, and settings to discover what works best for your style. Use these tips and settings as your starting point to enhance the visual impact of your Roblox experiences and promotional materials.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFeel free to experiment and share any of these tips and settings. Leave a comment letting us know if these tips are helpful or if there are any other settings or tips you’ve found helpful in showcasing your content!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch1\u003e\n\u003ca name=\"obs-settings-8\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#obs-settings-8\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eOBS Settings\u003c/h1\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOBS is a free and open-sourced video recording software available for all operating systems. Once you’ve installed OBS, you may need to adjust a few settings to ensure that your video looks as good as possible.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn OBS, navigate to File \u0026gt; Settings and use the following setting recommendations to get the most out of your screen captures.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch4\u003e\n\u003ca name=\"output-tab-9\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#output-tab-9\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eOutput Tab\u003c/h4\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSet Output Mode to Advanced to access additional settings.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eNavigate to the Recording tab.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSet Type to Standard.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSet Recording Path to your desired local directory.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSet Recording format to MPEG-4 (.mp4) or MOV (.mov) for Mac.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIf using an Nvidia graphics card, set Video Encoder to NVIDIA NVENC H.264\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIf using an AMD graphics card, set Video Encoder to x264.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSet Rate Control to CBR.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSet Bitrate to 20000 kbps as a minimum. You may want to increase later based on performance.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSet Preset to P4: Medium (Medium Quality). You may want to increase later based on performance.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSet Tuning to High Quality.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSet Multipass Mode to Single Pass. You may want to increase this later based on performance.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSet Profile to main.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cimg src=\"/secure-uploads/uploads/original/5X/b/8/1/3/b813c517f6786d2715f4820a16fd22a63ab23c12.png\" alt=\"\" data-base62-sha1=\"qgqd6vIp0SgiO7djGVwXJi8jlqa\" width=\"499\" height=\"499\" role=\"presentation\"\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003ch4\u003e\n\u003ca name=\"video-tab-10\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#video-tab-10\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eVideo Tab\u003c/h4\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSet Base (Canvas) Resolution to 3840x2160 for 4k capture. For smaller screens, reduce this to your primary monitor’s resolution.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSet Output (Scaled) Resolution to 3840x2160 for 4k capture. For smaller screens, reduce this to your primary monitor’s resolution.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSet Common FPS Values to 60.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cimg src=\"/secure-uploads/uploads/original/5X/d/3/a/b/d3abce89c88abaa551a24ff75ff212dbdef3dd2a.png\" alt=\"\" data-base62-sha1=\"ucwQ7jYcIM82PSQuHU8wiRCK8hs\" width=\"499\" height=\"500\" role=\"presentation\"\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003ch4\u003e\n\u003ca name=\"advanced-tab-11\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#advanced-tab-11\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eAdvanced Tab\u003c/h4\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSet Filename Formatting to your own file naming convention, such as RBLX_ProjectName_ShotType_ShotName.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cimg src=\"/secure-uploads/uploads/original/5X/3/e/f/3/3ef3e5417feaaf91d832b6ff194f4995e4454313.png\" alt=\"\" data-base62-sha1=\"8YU96O6FGVER8AdJ0pvpJXC3eSv\" width=\"530\" height=\"500\" role=\"presentation\"\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003ch4\u003e\n\u003ca name=\"setting-scenes-and-source-capture-12\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#setting-scenes-and-source-capture-12\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSetting Scenes and Source Capture\u003c/h4\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUse the following steps to create your scene and recording sources:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn the OBS main window, navigate to the Sources panel and select the + icon.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cimg src=\"/secure-uploads/uploads/original/5X/2/2/a/a/22aa8d53a9495c40b792e0570a5d82e8868634b0.png\" alt=\"\" data-base62-sha1=\"4WFDGwiI9mVf6BjzfxX7WimcJWM\" width=\"539\" height=\"500\" role=\"presentation\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSelect Display Capture.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cimg src=\"/secure-uploads/uploads/original/5X/f/8/5/0/f850c668becbd85af1d0d68a3c1d91a6335d152e.png\" alt=\"\" data-base62-sha1=\"zqHthR8REtnIndsshlRrg02gZNY\" width=\"313\" height=\"499\" role=\"presentation\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn the new Create/Select Source popup, set a name for your display source.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cimg src=\"/secure-uploads/uploads/original/5X/7/1/5/0/71507539692b70c4a00c7a14791cb9aecded230a.png\" alt=\"\" data-base62-sha1=\"gaqkJywt6JKiLVIn6rXxgF4bjTA\" width=\"510\" height=\"499\" role=\"presentation\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSet DISPLAY to your display source.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf you want to prevent OBS from capturing your cursor, set Capture Cursor to Off.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eClick OK when complete.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn the Sources panel, click the + button and select Audio Capture Device.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cimg src=\"/secure-uploads/uploads/original/5X/c/7/6/6/c7665649d2b4fa0ab5af3ed7a1ca37448e2e7a59.png\" alt=\"\" data-base62-sha1=\"srYgUwaQN8grkF7WevniRSDmBPH\" width=\"315\" height=\"500\" role=\"presentation\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSelect Create New and name the source for your audio import.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cimg src=\"/secure-uploads/uploads/original/5X/9/2/7/2/927284037b8409ea31e44a6a0038280829f5b4ae.png\" alt=\"\" data-base62-sha1=\"kTx3Gjma3FHM31PJPxavna3oLHo\" width=\"511\" height=\"500\" role=\"presentation\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDouble click your new source and set the Device to your computer’s current audio device.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cimg src=\"/secure-uploads/uploads/original/5X/e/3/4/c/e34c913b95af4483725b2b7847b870d02a11e396.png\" alt=\"\" data-base62-sha1=\"wqMqGShcAhpKCCOXTHLzU98cpMi\" width=\"690\" height=\"199\" role=\"presentation\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith these quick settings, you can now begin recording your screen and audio by pressing the Start Recording button.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":6,"updated_at":"2024-02-13T20:00:00.000Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":10786,"reads":1573,"readers_count":1572,"score":54749.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":2723897,"topic_slug":"tips-for-capturing-high-quality-screenshots-and-videos-in-studio","display_username":"blutzer","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":13,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://obsproject.com/","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Open Broadcaster Software | OBS","clicks":95},{"url":"https://devforum.roblox.com/secure-uploads/uploads/original/5X/a/0/5/b/a05b10eee87d04c32869997ccc1066cf2b02ddef.jpeg","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"a05b10eee87d04c32869997ccc1066cf2b02ddef.jpeg","clicks":0},{"url":"https://devforum.roblox.com/secure-uploads/uploads/original/5X/8/5/1/d/851d0ac23063c959651aabfbbfb2ac23640eb58d.jpeg","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"851d0ac23063c959651aabfbbfb2ac23640eb58d.jpeg","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":38}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":379979,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/tips-for-capturing-high-quality-screenshots-and-videos-in-studio/2723897/1","can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_translate":false,"is_translated":false,"detected_language":null},{"id":10432483,"name":"sneaksie","username":"Sneaksie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/devforum.roblox.com/sneaksie/{size}/6274570_2.png","created_at":"2024-02-29T21:22:53.364Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eexcellent tutorial! just want to add on about recording in OBS:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMP4 has bad error recovery. if you’re recording in .mp4 format and your OBS crashes for whatever reason, you may lose that entire video. I suggest setting your recording format to .mkv and then remux the recording to .mp4.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOBS can do this automatically for you by navigating to File \u0026gt; Settings and in the Advanced tab, tick the box for Automatically remux to mp4\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":2,"post_type":1,"posts_count":6,"updated_at":"2024-02-29T21:22:53.364Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":20,"reads":662,"readers_count":661,"score":382.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":2723897,"topic_slug":"tips-for-capturing-high-quality-screenshots-and-videos-in-studio","display_username":"sneaksie","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":10}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":29542,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/tips-for-capturing-high-quality-screenshots-and-videos-in-studio/2723897/2","can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_translate":false,"is_translated":false,"detected_language":null},{"id":10440654,"name":"PrizeCP","username":"PrizeCounterPuncher","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/devforum.roblox.com/prizecounterpuncher/{size}/6102082_2.png","created_at":"2024-03-02T21:11:58.005Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eAwesome tips.  Thank you.  Can’t wait to try them out.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":3,"post_type":1,"posts_count":6,"updated_at":"2024-03-02T21:11:58.005Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":8,"reads":599,"readers_count":598,"score":159.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":2723897,"topic_slug":"tips-for-capturing-high-quality-screenshots-and-videos-in-studio","display_username":"PrizeCP","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":692420,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/tips-for-capturing-high-quality-screenshots-and-videos-in-studio/2723897/3","can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_translate":false,"is_translated":false,"detected_language":null},{"id":10742393,"name":"m2thedeep","username":"m2thedeep","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/devforum.roblox.com/m2thedeep/{size}/5481431_2.png","created_at":"2024-05-07T23:08:47.966Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eGreat write-up! Thanks for posting this. The video quality of OBS is quite poor out of the box, so this guide is extremely helpful for those looking for high quality videos.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":4,"post_type":1,"posts_count":6,"updated_at":"2024-05-07T23:08:47.966Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":5,"reads":452,"readers_count":451,"score":115.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":2723897,"topic_slug":"tips-for-capturing-high-quality-screenshots-and-videos-in-studio","display_username":"m2thedeep","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":1548545,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/tips-for-capturing-high-quality-screenshots-and-videos-in-studio/2723897/4","can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_translate":false,"is_translated":false,"detected_language":null},{"id":10743080,"name":"SwitchedDreams","username":"SwitchedDreams","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/devforum.roblox.com/switcheddreams/{size}/9074242_2.png","created_at":"2024-05-08T03:35:58.858Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eThe new UI seems to have a problem; The Roblox icon in the top left corner stays visible, unlike previous ones.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNot sure if its intentional, but it does not look good in a promotional video, it looks like Roblox is watermarking my video.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePlus, it forces me to crop the video, which is valuable footage that is being cut away. Any fixes for that planned anytime soon?\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":5,"post_type":1,"posts_count":6,"updated_at":"2024-05-08T03:35:58.858Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":17,"reads":397,"readers_count":396,"score":179.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":2723897,"topic_slug":"tips-for-capturing-high-quality-screenshots-and-videos-in-studio","display_username":"SwitchedDreams","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":"Builders","flair_url":"hammer","flair_bg_color":"E5BF00","flair_color":"fff","flair_group_id":53,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"Builder","title_is_group":false,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":546657,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"de